## Rule 1 — Never Hardcode Credentials

Keystore passwords, key aliases, service account JSON, and signing key material are **never** committed. Read them from `local.properties` (developer machine) or environment variables (CI). The keystore binary itself is never committed; on CI it is base64-decoded into `${runner.temp}` and shredded after use.

```
# .gitignore — must contain
local.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
play-service-account.json
```

```properties
# local.properties — developer machine ONLY, gitignored
sdk.dir=/Users/you/Library/Android/sdk
RELEASE_STORE_FILE=/Users/you/keystores/example-release.jks
RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD=********
RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS=example-release
RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD=********
```

```kotlin
// app/build.gradle.kts — read local.properties safely
import java.util.Properties

val localProps = Properties().apply {
    val f = rootProject.file("local.properties")
    if (f.exists()) f.inputStream().use { load(it) }
}

fun prop(name: String): String? =
    localProps.getProperty(name) ?: System.getenv(name)
```

