## Rule 4 — Version Management

Treat `versionName` as semantic (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`) and `versionCode` as a strictly monotonic integer. Drive both from a single source of truth — `libs.versions.toml` for the name; git commit count or CI build number for the code.

```toml
# gradle/libs.versions.toml
[versions]
app-version-name = "1.4.2"
```

```kotlin
// app/build.gradle.kts
import org.gradle.api.GradleException

fun gitCommitCount(): Int =
    try {
        val process = ProcessBuilder("git", "rev-list", "--count", "HEAD")
            .redirectErrorStream(true)
            .start()
        process.inputStream.bufferedReader().readText().trim().toInt()
            .also { process.waitFor() }
    } catch (e: Exception) {
        throw GradleException("Failed to compute versionCode from git: ${e.message}")
    }

android {
    defaultConfig {
        // CI build number wins on CI, git commit count locally — both monotonic
        versionCode = System.getenv("CI_BUILD_NUMBER")?.toIntOrNull() ?: gitCommitCount()
        versionName = libs.versions.app.version.name.get()
    }
}
```

**Bump policy (driven by Conventional Commits since the last tag):**

| Commits include | Bump |
|---|---|
| `feat!:` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer | MAJOR |
| `feat:` (no breaking) | MINOR |
| `fix:`, `perf:`, `refactor:`, etc. only | PATCH |

```bash
# /release prepare — fully scripted bump
LAST_TAG=$(git describe --tags --abbrev=0)
git log "$LAST_TAG"..HEAD --pretty=format:"%s" > /tmp/commits.txt

# Decide bump
if grep -qE "^(feat!|fix!|.*BREAKING CHANGE)" /tmp/commits.txt; then BUMP=major
elif grep -qE "^feat(\(|:)" /tmp/commits.txt;                       then BUMP=minor
else                                                                     BUMP=patch
fi
echo "Detected bump: $BUMP"

# Edit libs.versions.toml manually OR use a tool like semantic-release / cz-cli
```

Never reset `versionCode`. Even for a major version bump it keeps incrementing — the Play Store rejects uploads with a `versionCode` less than or equal to the current production track.

