## Rule 5 — App Bundle (AAB) vs APK

**Always ship AAB to the Play Store.** Universal APKs exist only for GitHub Releases, sideloading, and Firebase App Distribution.

| Format | When | Task |
|---|---|---|
| `.aab` (App Bundle) | Play Store, App Signing required | `./gradlew bundleRelease` |
| Split APKs (per-ABI / per-density) | Stores that don't accept AAB (Amazon, Samsung Galaxy Store) | `./gradlew assembleRelease` |
| Universal APK | GitHub Releases, manual sideload, QA distribution | enable in `bundle { ... }` block, extracted from AAB via `bundletool` |

```kotlin
// app/build.gradle.kts — control AAB splits and ship a universal APK alongside it
android {
    bundle {
        language { enableSplit = true }
        density  { enableSplit = true }
        abi      { enableSplit = true }
    }

    // Generates a universal APK as part of bundleRelease — handy for GitHub releases
    splits {
        abi {
            isEnable = true
            reset()
            include("armeabi-v7a", "arm64-v8a", "x86_64")
            isUniversalApk = true
        }
    }
}
```

```bash
# Build outputs
./gradlew bundleRelease        # → app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab
./gradlew assembleRelease      # → app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-*.apk

# Extract install-ready APKs from an AAB for verification
bundletool build-apks \
  --bundle=app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab \
  --output=app-release.apks \
  --mode=universal \
  --ks=example-release.jks \
  --ks-key-alias=example-release
```

