## Rule 6 — R8 Full Mode Verification

R8 full mode is mandatory for release. Verify shrinking actually happened — empty `mapping.txt` or a release APK the same size as debug means something silently disabled it.

```properties
# gradle.properties — checked into repo
android.enableR8.fullMode=true
```

```kotlin
// app/build.gradle.kts
android {
    buildTypes {
        release {
            isMinifyEnabled   = true
            isShrinkResources = true
            proguardFiles(
                getDefaultProguardFile("proguard-android-optimize.txt"),
                "proguard-rules.pro",
            )
        }
    }
}
```

```bash
# After bundleRelease, verify R8 did its job
./gradlew bundleRelease

# 1. mapping.txt should exist and contain thousands of obfuscated lines
wc -l app/build/outputs/mapping/release/mapping.txt
# expect: 50000+ lines on a real app; if 0 or missing → R8 didn't run

# 2. Resource shrinking report should show removed resources
cat app/build/outputs/mapping/release/resources.txt | head -50

# 3. Compare AAB size to a debug APK — release should be significantly smaller
ls -lh app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab
ls -lh app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk

# 4. Decompile a sample class to confirm obfuscation
unzip -p app-release.aab base/dex/classes.dex | head -c 200 | xxd | head -5

# 5. Symbolicate a stack trace — required for crash reporting
retrace app/build/outputs/mapping/release/mapping.txt < obfuscated-stacktrace.txt
```

Upload `mapping.txt` to Play Console and Crashlytics on every release — Gradle Play Publisher and the Crashlytics plugin do this automatically when configured.

