## Rule 7 — Gradle Play Publisher

Use [Gradle Play Publisher](https://github.com/Triple-T/gradle-play-publisher) to ship from CI. It handles AAB upload, mapping file upload, listing assets, and track promotion.

```toml
# gradle/libs.versions.toml
[versions]
play-publisher = "3.12.1"

[plugins]
play-publisher = { id = "com.github.triplet.play", version.ref = "play-publisher" }
```

```kotlin
// app/build.gradle.kts
plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.android.application)
    alias(libs.plugins.play.publisher)
}

play {
    // Path to a GCP service account JSON with "Release Manager" role on the Play Console app
    serviceAccountCredentials.set(
        rootProject.file(prop("PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON_PATH") ?: "play-service-account.json")
    )

    track.set("internal")                // internal → alpha → beta → production
    releaseStatus.set(com.github.triplet.gradle.androidpublisher.ReleaseStatus.COMPLETED)
    defaultToAppBundles.set(true)        // always upload AAB, never APK
    artifactDir.set(file("build/outputs/bundle/release"))

    // Staged rollout — start at 10% on production
    userFractionEnabled.set(false)       // set true for staged rollouts
    // userFraction.set(0.1)             // 10% rollout

    // Release notes — read from fastlane/metadata/android/<locale>/changelogs/<versionCode>.txt
    // Gradle Play Publisher picks these up automatically
}
```

```
fastlane/metadata/android/
  en-US/
    title.txt
    short_description.txt
    full_description.txt
    changelogs/
      142.txt          # release notes for versionCode 142
      143.txt
```

**Tasks:**

```bash
# Upload to internal track (fast review, ~minutes)
./gradlew publishReleaseBundle

# Promote internal → alpha (no rebuild — Play Store just moves the artifact)
./gradlew promoteArtifact --from-track internal --promote-track alpha

# Promote alpha → beta
./gradlew promoteArtifact --from-track alpha --promote-track beta

# Promote beta → production with a 10% staged rollout
./gradlew promoteArtifact --from-track beta --promote-track production --user-fraction 0.1

# Increase rollout
./gradlew promoteArtifact --from-track production --user-fraction 0.5
./gradlew promoteArtifact --from-track production --user-fraction 1.0
```

**Service account setup (one-time, in GCP Console):**
1. Create a service account in your GCP project.
2. Grant it the role `Service Account User` in GCP IAM.
3. In Play Console → Settings → API access → invite the service account email.
4. Grant it **Release Manager** permission on the specific app (not org-wide).
5. Download the JSON key; store as `PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` CI secret.

