## Rule 9 — Conventional Commits Changelog

`CHANGELOG.md` is regenerated by `/release prepare` from commit messages since the last tag. Follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com) format and [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) parsing.

```markdown
# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

## [1.4.2] - 2026-05-26

### Added
- User profile editing screen (#142)
- Offline-first sync for saved articles (#138)

### Fixed
- Crash on cold start when locale is unset (#145)
- Memory leak in image loading on configuration change (#147)

### Changed
- Bumped compileSdk to 35
- Migrated DataStore from Preferences to Proto

### Security
- Bumped okhttp to 4.12.0 (CVE-2023-3635)

[Unreleased]: https://github.com/example/app/compare/v1.4.2...HEAD
[1.4.2]: https://github.com/example/app/compare/v1.4.1...v1.4.2
```

**Commit-to-section mapping:**

| Commit prefix | CHANGELOG section |
|---|---|
| `feat:` | Added |
| `fix:` | Fixed |
| `perf:`, `refactor:` | Changed |
| `security:`, `fix(deps):` for CVEs | Security |
| `chore:`, `docs:`, `style:`, `test:`, `ci:`, `build:` | Omitted from CHANGELOG (visible only in git log) |
| `feat!:` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer | Listed under "Breaking Changes" at top |

