## Pre-Release Checklist (`/release` default)

Run through every item; any unchecked item blocks the release.

### Code & Build
- [ ] `versionName` bumped per SemVer rules in `libs.versions.toml`
- [ ] `versionCode` strictly greater than current production track
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` regenerated and reviewed
- [ ] `applicationId` matches the Play Console app (no debug suffix)
- [ ] `minSdk`, `targetSdk`, `compileSdk` reviewed against Play target API requirements
- [ ] All `TODO`, `FIXME`, `STOPSHIP` comments resolved or filed as issues

### Signing
- [ ] Release keystore exists and is backed up in encrypted storage
- [ ] `local.properties` keystore entries present locally (never committed)
- [ ] CI secrets configured: `RELEASE_KEYSTORE_BASE64`, `RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD`, `RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS`, `RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD`
- [ ] `signingConfig` wired into the release build type — `./gradlew assembleRelease` produces a signed APK
- [ ] `apksigner verify --verbose --print-certs app-release.apk` confirms v2 + v3 signatures present
- [ ] Play App Signing enrolled for this `applicationId`

### Manifest & Runtime
- [ ] `android:debuggable` not set in manifest (Gradle owns it)
- [ ] `android:allowBackup="false"` (or backup rules explicitly defined)
- [ ] `android:usesCleartextTraffic="false"`
- [ ] `networkSecurityConfig` defined; production hosts pinned where required
- [ ] No `Log.d` / `Log.v` reachable in release — Timber `DebugTree` not planted, ProGuard strips `Log.*`
- [ ] StrictMode disabled in release
- [ ] LeakCanary, Chucker, Flipper, debug HTTP loggers excluded from release variant

### R8 / Shrinking
- [ ] `isMinifyEnabled = true` and `isShrinkResources = true` for release
- [ ] `android.enableR8.fullMode=true` in `gradle.properties`
- [ ] `proguard-rules.pro` covers Retrofit/OkHttp, kotlinx.serialization, Room, your DI framework, and any reflection-based libraries
- [ ] `mapping.txt` generated and non-empty after `bundleRelease`
- [ ] Smoke test the signed AAB via `bundletool` install-apks on a real device

### Tests & Quality
- [ ] All unit tests green: `./gradlew testReleaseUnitTest`
- [ ] All instrumented tests green on the release variant
- [ ] `./gradlew lint` zero warnings; ktlint + Detekt clean
- [ ] `./gradlew checkReleaseBadging` passes (no unintended hardware-feature requirements)
- [ ] Baseline Profile regenerated if startup-critical code changed

### Play Store
- [ ] Gradle Play Publisher `serviceAccountCredentials` configured
- [ ] Fastlane metadata directory exists with current `changelogs/<versionCode>.txt` for every active locale
- [ ] Screenshots up to date for all required form factors (phone, 7" tablet, 10" tablet, foldable)
- [ ] Data safety form reviewed in Play Console
- [ ] Internal track upload succeeded; QA installed via Play internal link
- [ ] `mapping.txt` uploaded (automatic via Gradle Play Publisher)

### Crash Reporting
- [ ] Crashlytics / Sentry / your reporter initialised in release `Application.onCreate`
- [ ] `mapping.txt` symbolication enabled; verified with a test crash from a release build
- [ ] User identifier scrubbing reviewed (no PII attached to crash reports)

### GitHub
- [ ] Tag pushed in the form `vX.Y.Z` from `main` after merge
- [ ] `release.yml` succeeded; GitHub Release created with AAB, universal APK, and `mapping.txt` attached
- [ ] Release notes match `CHANGELOG.md` section

### Post-Release Monitoring (first 24h)
- [ ] Crash-free user rate above release-gate threshold (e.g., > 99.5%)
- [ ] ANR rate below threshold
- [ ] No spike in 5xx from backend
- [ ] Staged rollout halted automatically if Vitals thresholds breached

